# Navigation

- `createNativeStackNavigator<RootStackParamList>()` with the dynamic API; screens `Posts` and `DetailsScreen`.
- `RootStackParamList` lives in `src/shared/config/routes.ts`, which also augments `ReactNavigation.RootParamList` inside `declare global`.
- Params carry ids only: `DetailsScreen: { postId: number }`.
- Only `src/app/navigation` and `src/pages` use React Navigation. Widgets, features and entities get callbacks such as `onPostPress(postId)`.
- Pages are typed with `NativeStackScreenProps<RootStackParamList, 'DetailsScreen'>`; route names are checked keys of the param list.
- Native headers titled "PostsScreen" and "DetailsScreen"; theme, `headerTintColor` and `headerTitleStyle` from tokens.
- `NavigationContainer` lives in `RootNavigator`; no state persistence, no deep links.

Checks:
- `tsc` for route names and params (enabled).
- ESLint `no-restricted-imports` for `@react-navigation/*` outside allowed folders (enabled).

Full guide: @docs/ai/guidelines/navigation.md
